  "description": "DOFQIC crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group I 2/a. Reported CIF formula moiety: C61 H67 Cl4 Dy4 N9 O11,2(C2 H6 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 4 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 3 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.541-3.869 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.39-110.92°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy4(H2Lr)3(Cl)4(μ3-O)(EtOH)2(H2O)2]·2EtOH·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
